{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014w7UvCZGxgqA8RRTad32sJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation\n2\t\n3\tReplace per-AIR `interpolate_columns_gpu` kernel launches in MLE sumcheck rounds with a single batched descriptor-array kernel per round. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~310 AIRs (at APC 300), issuing a separate `cudaMallocAsync` + H2D column-pointer upload + kernel launch per AIR. Nsys profiling shows 4993 total `interpolate_columns_kernel` launches with only 20ms GPU compute time, indicating that allocation and launch overhead (~60-80ms) dominates the 180ms MLE Rounds span. Batching these into one kernel launch per round using the descriptor-array pattern (proven in batch-stacking-scatter and batch-mle-round-kernels) should reduce this overhead to ~5-10ms.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50386b42-eb75-4189-9b73-2a1359832805","uuid":"e2c285c5-29e5-42b9-82ea-94616677ede0","timestamp":"2026-04-13T09:28:08.104Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation\n\nReplace per-AIR `interpolate_columns_gpu` kernel launches in MLE sumcheck rounds with a single batched descriptor-array kernel per round. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~310 AIRs (at APC 300), issuing a separate `cudaMallocAsync` + H2D column-pointer upload + kernel launch per AIR. Nsys profiling shows 4993 total `interpolate_columns_kernel` launches with only 20ms GPU compute time, indicating that allocation and launch overhead (~60-80ms) dominates the 180ms MLE Rounds span. Batching these into one kernel launch per round using the descriptor-array pattern (proven in batch-stacking-scatter and batch-mle-round-kernels) should reduce this overhead to ~5-10ms.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
