erkle tree via `MerkleTreeGpu::new_with_hash::<MH>()`\n  - This triggers row hashing (expensive) followed by layer compression (cheaper)\n\n### Recommendations:\n\n1. **If you need to find the kernel name**, check the build logs from the optimization run:\n   - `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/logs/20260413-112757-12-1-plan.log`\n   - This mentions 584 calls with 187.7μs average latency\n\n2. **Potential optimization opportunities** (based on code analysis):\n   - The `bn254_zero_init()` and similar zero initializations could be cached if zeros are constant\n   - Merkle tree layer compression (`compress_layer` calls) applies Poseidon2 to adjacent pairs - these results could theoretically be precomputed for the zero tree\n   - The 584 kernel calls suggest high launch overhead - could benefit from kernel fusion or batching\n\n3. **To confirm identity**:\n   - Run `nsys` profile with CUDA kernel function name collection enabled\n   - Check PTX assembly in the built `.a` library file  \n   - Compare commit history to find when the kernel was added/removed\n\nWould you like me to search for additional context in the profiling logs or check specific optimization opportunities?"}],"totalDurationMs":108007,"totalTokens":68998,"totalToolUseCount":63,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":227,"cache_read_input_tokens":67552,"output_tokens":1219,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":227},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1219,"cache_read_input_tokens":67552,"cache_creation_input_tokens":227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":227,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":15,"searchCount":9,"bashCount":39,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
