{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015Yzxq88VtVq17Pucfcx2tc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018j3JizcnzbXCEKoomf1CWw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-1430-batch-mle-main-ptrs-upload\n\nReplace per-trace `main_ptrs.to_device()` calls in MLE sumcheck rounds with a single batched device upload per round. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~310 traces (at APC 300) and calls `main_ptrs.to_device()` individually, issuing a separate `cudaMallocAsync` + `cudaMemcpyAsync` for a tiny buffer (~16-48 bytes) per trace. Across ~8 rounds per segment and 2 segments, this totals ~5000 unnecessary allocation+copy pairs. Consolidating all per-round main_ptrs into a single flat vector and uploading once eliminates this overhead, saving an estimated 30-50ms from the 170ms MLE Rounds span at APC 300.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1143,"cache_read_input_tokens":116587,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1143},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50386b42-eb75-4189-9b73-2a1359832805","uuid":"4caaced3-22aa-4836-a0eb-8f829259de17"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018j3JizcnzbXCEKoomf1CWw","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50386b42-eb75-4189-9b73-2a1359832805","uuid":"077f36ec-56ec-47c5-9da8-0664ce1a97cf","timestamp":"2026-04-13T09:43:20.085Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-1430-batch-mle-main-ptrs-upload\n\nReplace per-trace `main_ptrs.to_device()` calls in MLE sumcheck rounds with a single batched device upload per round. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~310 traces (at APC 300) and calls `main_ptrs.to_device()` individually, issuing a separate `cudaMallocAsync` + `cudaMemcpyAsync` for a tiny buffer (~16-48 bytes) per trace. Across ~8 rounds per segment and 2 segments, this totals ~5000 unnecessary allocation+copy pairs. Consolidating all per-round main_ptrs into a single flat vector and uploading once eliminates this overhead, saving an estimated 30-50ms from the 170ms MLE Rounds span at APC 300.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":["-# 2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation","+# 2026-04-13-1430-batch-mle-main-ptrs-upload"," ","-Replace per-AIR `interpolate_columns_gpu` kernel launches in MLE sumcheck rounds with a single batched descriptor-array kernel per round. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~310 AIRs (at APC 300), issuing a separate `cudaMallocAsync` + H2D column-pointer upload + kernel launch per AIR. Nsys profiling shows 4993 total `interpolate_columns_kernel` launches with only 20ms GPU compute time, indicating that allocation and launch overhead (~60-80ms) dominates the 180ms MLE Rounds span. Batching these into one kernel launch per round using the descriptor-array pattern (proven in batch-stacking-scatter and batch-mle-round-kernels) should reduce this overhead to ~5-10ms.","+Replace per-trace `main_ptrs.to_device()` calls in MLE sumcheck rounds with a single batched device upload per round. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~310 traces (at APC 300) and calls `main_ptrs.to_device()` individually, issuing a separate `cudaMallocAsync` + `cudaMemcpyAsync` for a tiny buffer (~16-48 bytes) per trace. Across ~8 rounds per segment and 2 segments, this totals ~5000 unnecessary allocation+copy pairs. Consolidating all per-round main_ptrs into a single flat vector and uploading once eliminates this overhead, saving an estimated 30-50ms from the 170ms MLE Rounds span at APC 300."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-13-1100-batch-mle-interpolation\n\nReplace per-AIR `interpolate_columns_gpu` kernel launches in MLE sumcheck rounds with a single batched descriptor-array kernel per round. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~310 AIRs (at APC 300), issuing a separate `cudaMallocAsync` + H2D column-pointer upload + kernel launch per AIR. Nsys profiling shows 4993 total `interpolate_columns_kernel` launches with only 20ms GPU compute time, indicating that allocation and launch overhead (~60-80ms) dominates the 180ms MLE Rounds span. Batching these into one kernel launch per round using the descriptor-array pattern (proven in batch-stacking-scatter and batch-mle-round-kernels) should reduce this overhead to ~5-10ms.\n"}}
