{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019EQkZZMbJp1Bm78KixczKB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-1430-batch-mle-main-ptrs-upload\n2\t\n3\tReplace per-trace `main_ptrs.to_device()` calls in MLE sumcheck rounds with a single batched device upload per round. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~310 traces (at APC 300) and calls `main_ptrs.to_device()` individually, issuing a separate `cudaMallocAsync` + `cudaMemcpyAsync` for a tiny buffer (~16-48 bytes) per trace. Across ~8 rounds per segment and 2 segments, this totals ~5000 unnecessary allocation+copy pairs. Consolidating all per-round main_ptrs into a single flat vector and uploading once eliminates this overhead, saving an estimated 30-50ms from the 170ms MLE Rounds span at APC 300.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rvg4ZQaVH5J2HLreKE5UF2","session_id":"50386b42-eb75-4189-9b73-2a1359832805","uuid":"f4727c49-f506-49d7-9fce-6c233956d0df","timestamp":"2026-04-13T09:44:55.507Z"}
